window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b260-5d479a820c951a6d.json"]={sha256:"5d479a820c951a6d31c988e46e8fe180493eda250816f558c703e753c5adf123",value:{"id":"b260","title":"調壓井水錘控制","titleEn":"Surge-shaft control of water hammer","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課將快速彈性壓力波與較慢的調壓井自由水面振盪分開建模，再用共同邊界把兩者連起來。十個單元涵蓋波速、往返時間、首波增量、井內連續方程、剛性水柱週期、無損湧升、摩擦節流、汽化及數值收斂，所有算例都明定原創假設，不提供可直接套用的閥門動作規程。","summaryEn":"This course models rapid elastic pressure waves separately from slower free-surface surge oscillations, then reconnects them through shared boundaries. Ten units cover celerity, travel time, first-wave increment, continuity, rigid-column period, ideal upsurge, friction, throttling, vapor formation and numerical convergence. All examples state original assumptions rather than prescribing transferable valve-operating procedures.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["彈性波速與管壁","Elastic wave speed and pipe wall"],["快速變速壓力增量","Rapid velocity-change pressure"],["剛性水柱振盪週期","Rigid-column oscillation period"],["節流孔與局部損失","Throttle opening and local loss"],["特徵網格與收斂","Characteristic grid and convergence"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["彈性波速與管壁","快速變速壓力增量","剛性水柱振盪週期","節流孔與局部損失","特徵網格與收斂"],"labelsEn":["Elastic wave speed and pipe wall","Rapid velocity-change pressure","Rigid-column oscillation period","Throttle opening and local loss","Characteristic grid and convergence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創井面積敏感度：定水位上庫、無損剛性水柱、初始井位與庫位相同，L=1000m、Ap=10m²、V0=2m/s且瞬停下游時，As=100m²得到zmax=6.3855m。將井面積增加10%至110m²而其他假設不變，湧升變為6.3855/√1.1≈6.0883m，降低約4.65%，並非10%。同時理想週期會乘√1.1而變長。學徒應比較較低湧升與較長振盪的不同效果，再加入摩擦、井水慣性、通氣及彈性管路，不把理想幅值減少誤稱所有壓力風險均以相同比例降低。","textEn":"Original shaft-area sensitivity: assume a fixed reservoir, lossless rigid column, equal initial shaft and reservoir levels,L=1000m,Ap=10m²,V0=2m/s and instantaneous downstream demand stop. Shaft area100m² gives maximum rise6.3855m. Increasing area10% to110m² with all other assumptions fixed gives6.3855/√1.1≈6.0883m, about4.65% lower rather than10%. The ideal period simultaneously increases by√1.1. Apprentices compare lower rise with longer oscillation before adding friction, shaft inertia, ventilation and elastic waterways. A reduced ideal amplitude does not imply that every pressure risk declines by the same percentage across the full connected system.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b260-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「彈性波速與管壁」與「往返時間與邊界」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall\" and \"Round-trip time and boundaries\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b260-v15-01","title":"彈性波速與管壁：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「彈性波速與管壁」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水錘傳播速度同時受水可壓縮性與管壁變形影響，不是把水視為完全剛性就能描述。管壁約束、材料模數與含氣量會改變波速，薄壁圓管公式需要明列修正係數；用一個假設波速計算的壓力峰值，必須隨參數不確定度重新檢查。 假設K=2.2GPa、ρ=1000kg/m³、E=200GPa、D=2m、t=0.02m，管壁修正係數取1，a=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「彈性波速與管壁」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water-hammer propagation depends on both fluid compressibility and pipe-wall deformation, so a rigid-water assumption cannot describe the wave. Restraint, material modulus and gas content affect celerity, and the thin circular-pipe expression requires an explicit restraint factor. Pressure estimates made with one assumed speed must be reconsidered when that parameter is uncertain. AssumeK=2.2GPa,ρ=1000kg/m³,E=200GPa,D=2m,t=0.02m and wall-restraint factor1. Wave speeda=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s for this idealization. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「彈性波速與管壁」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-01-k1","title":"彈性波速與管壁","titleEn":"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall","text":"水錘傳播速度同時受水可壓縮性與管壁變形影響，不是把水視為完全剛性就能描述。管壁約束、材料模數與含氣量會改變波速，薄壁圓管公式需要明列修正係數；用一個假設波速計算的壓力峰值，必須隨參數不確定度重新檢查。","textEn":"Water-hammer propagation depends on both fluid compressibility and pipe-wall deformation, so a rigid-water assumption cannot describe the wave. Restraint, material modulus and gas content affect celerity, and the thin circular-pipe expression requires an explicit restraint factor.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「彈性波速與管壁」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall\" is correct?","options":["水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。","水錘傳播速度同時受水可壓縮性與管壁變形影響，不是把水視為完全剛性就能描述。","閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas.","Water-hammer propagation depends on both fluid compressibility and pipe-wall deformation, so a rigid-water assumption cannot describe the wave.","An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水錘傳播速度同時受水可壓縮性與管壁變形影響，不是把水視為完全剛性就能描述。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water-hammer propagation depends on both fluid compressibility and pipe-wall deformation, so a rigid-water assumption cannot describe the wave. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b260-v15-02","title":"彈性波速與管壁：定量估算","titleEn":"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「彈性波速與管壁」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設K=2.2GPa、ρ=1000kg/m³、E=200GPa、D=2m、t=0.02m，管壁修正係數取1，a=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. AssumeK=2.2GPa,ρ=1000kg/m³,E=200GPa,D=2m,t=0.02m and wall-restraint factor1. Wave speeda=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s for this idealization. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設K=2.2GPa、ρ=1000kg/m³、E=200GPa、D=2m、t=0.02m，管壁修正係數取1，a=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. AssumeK=2.2GPa,ρ=1000kg/m³,E=200GPa,D=2m,t=0.02m and wall-restraint factor1. Wave speeda=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s for this idealization.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「彈性波速與管壁」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall\", which statement holds?","options":["瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。","理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow.","The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b260-v15-03","title":"彈性波速與管壁：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「彈性波速與管壁」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。用量測波到達時間比較估計波速，再測試含氣或厚度變動的敏感度，不藉調整波速掩蓋錯誤邊界。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor. Compare predicted speed with measured wave arrival, then test gas-content and wall variations rather than tuning celerity to conceal an incorrect boundary condition. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。用量測波到達時間比較估計波速，再測試含氣或厚度變動的敏感度，不藉調整波速掩蓋錯誤邊界。","observationEn":"Site practice: Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor. Compare predicted speed with measured wave arrival, then test gas-content and wall variations rather than tuning celerity to conceal an incorrect boundary condition.","failure":"注意干擾：少量夾氣可能顯著改變可壓縮性，複合管或厚壁管也不符合簡式。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Entrained gas changes compressibility, and composite or thick walls fall outside this simple expression. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。用量測波到達時間比較估計波速，再測試含氣或厚度變動的敏感度，不藉調整波速掩蓋錯誤邊界。","textEn":"Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor. Compare predicted speed with measured wave arrival, then test gas-content and wall variations rather than tuning celerity to conceal an incorrect boundary condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。用量測波到達時間比較估計波速，再測試含氣或厚度變動的敏感度，不藉調整波速掩蓋錯誤邊界。","textEn":"Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor. Compare predicted speed with measured wave arrival, then test gas-content and wall variations rather than tuning celerity to conceal an incorrect boundary condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「彈性波速與管壁」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall\"?","options":["記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。"],"optionsEn":["Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system."],"answer":0,"explanation":"記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b260-v15-04","title":"彈性波速與管壁：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「彈性波速與管壁」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"少量夾氣可能顯著改變可壓縮性，複合管或厚壁管也不符合簡式。把鋼材彈性模數當水體積模數，或漏掉帕與吉帕換算，會使壓力與時間尺度同時失真。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Entrained gas changes compressibility, and composite or thick walls fall outside this simple expression. Substituting steel modulus for water bulk modulus or confusing pascals and gigapascals distorts both pressure magnitude and wave timing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設K=2.2GPa、ρ=1000kg/m³、E=200GPa、D=2m、t=0.02m，管壁修正係數取1，a=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Wave speeda=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s for this idealization.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"少量夾氣可能顯著改變可壓縮性，複合管或厚壁管也不符合簡式。把鋼材彈性模數當水體積模數，或漏掉帕與吉帕換算，會使壓力與時間尺度同時失真。","textEn":"Entrained gas changes compressibility, and composite or thick walls fall outside this simple expression. Substituting steel modulus for water bulk modulus or confusing pascals and gigapascals distorts both pressure magnitude and wave timing.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「彈性波速與管壁」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","少量夾氣可能顯著改變可壓縮性，複合管或厚壁管也不符合簡式。","閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Entrained gas changes compressibility, and composite or thick walls fall outside this simple expression.","An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"少量夾氣可能顯著改變可壓縮性，複合管或厚壁管也不符合簡式。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Entrained gas changes compressibility, and composite or thick walls fall outside this simple expression. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b260-v15-05","title":"往返時間與邊界：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Round-trip time and boundaries: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「往返時間與邊界」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Round-trip time and boundaries” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"閥門動作與壓力波往返時間的比較，決定反射是否已在動作期間返回控制點。最簡水庫管閥系統只有一條明確路徑，但分岔、調壓井與不同波速管段會產生多重反射；時間尺度只是辨識模型的入口，不能據此直接宣布某個關閉時間安全。 假設均勻管長L=1000m、波速a=1000m/s，往返時間2L/a=2s；只代表此單一路徑，不是允許關閉時間。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「往返時間與邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Comparing actuator duration with wave round-trip time shows whether a reflection returns during the action. A reservoir-pipe-valve system has one simple path, whereas branches, shafts and segments with different celerity create multiple reflections. This time scale helps select the analysis and does not by itself approve a particular valve-closing duration. Assume uniform pipe length1000m and celerity1000m/s. Round-trip2L/a=2s describes only this path, not an allowable closing time. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Round-trip time and boundaries” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「往返時間與邊界」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Round-trip time and boundaries”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-05-k1","title":"往返時間與邊界","titleEn":"Round-trip time and boundaries","text":"閥門動作與壓力波往返時間的比較，決定反射是否已在動作期間返回控制點。最簡水庫管閥系統只有一條明確路徑，但分岔、調壓井與不同波速管段會產生多重反射；時間尺度只是辨識模型的入口，不能據此直接宣布某個關閉時間安全。","textEn":"Comparing actuator duration with wave round-trip time shows whether a reflection returns during the action. A reservoir-pipe-valve system has one simple path, whereas branches, shafts and segments with different celerity create multiple reflections.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「往返時間與邊界」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Round-trip time and boundaries\" is correct?","options":["閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。","焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。","閥門動作與壓力波往返時間的比較，決定反射是否已在動作期間返回控制點。"],"optionsEn":["An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure.","The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.","Comparing actuator duration with wave round-trip time shows whether a reflection returns during the action."],"answer":2,"explanation":"閥門動作與壓力波往返時間的比較，決定反射是否已在動作期間返回控制點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Comparing actuator duration with wave round-trip time shows whether a reflection returns during the action. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b260-v15-06","title":"往返時間與邊界：定量估算","titleEn":"Round-trip time and boundaries: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「往返時間與邊界」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Round-trip time and boundaries” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設均勻管長L=1000m、波速a=1000m/s，往返時間2L/a=2s；只代表此單一路徑，不是允許關閉時間。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume uniform pipe length1000m and celerity1000m/s. Round-trip2L/a=2s describes only this path, not an allowable closing time. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設均勻管長L=1000m、波速a=1000m/s，往返時間2L/a=2s；只代表此單一路徑，不是允許關閉時間。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume uniform pipe length1000m and celerity1000m/s. Round-trip2L/a=2s describes only this path, not an allowable closing time.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「往返時間與邊界」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Round-trip time and boundaries\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。","管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time.","During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b260-v15-07","title":"往返時間與邊界：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Round-trip time and boundaries: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「往返時間與邊界」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Round-trip time and boundaries” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。遇到分岔或調壓接點就建立多路徑時間表，不能只取地圖上兩點直線距離。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories. For branches and shaft junctions construct a multiple-path timing table instead of using the straight-line distance between map locations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。遇到分岔或調壓接點就建立多路徑時間表，不能只取地圖上兩點直線距離。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories. For branches and shaft junctions construct a multiple-path timing table instead of using the straight-line distance between map locations.","failure":"注意干擾：將單程時間當往返時間會改變快速與慢速的分類，忽略分岔反射則可能漏掉疊加峰值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing one-way with round-trip time changes the rapid-action classification, while omitted branch reflections can hide superposed peaks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。遇到分岔或調壓接點就建立多路徑時間表，不能只取地圖上兩點直線距離。","textEn":"Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories. For branches and shaft junctions construct a multiple-path timing table instead of using the straight-line distance between map locations.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。遇到分岔或調壓接點就建立多路徑時間表，不能只取地圖上兩點直線距離。","textEn":"Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories. For branches and shaft junctions construct a multiple-path timing table instead of using the straight-line distance between map locations.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「往返時間與邊界」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Round-trip time and boundaries\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。","任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories.","Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b260-v15-08","title":"往返時間與邊界：失效診斷","titleEn":"Round-trip time and boundaries: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「往返時間與邊界」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Round-trip time and boundaries” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將單程時間當往返時間會改變快速與慢速的分類，忽略分岔反射則可能漏掉疊加峰值。即使動作很慢，長時間水位振盪或控制不穩定仍可能存在。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing one-way with round-trip time changes the rapid-action classification, while omitted branch reflections can hide superposed peaks. Slow actuation can still produce long-period level oscillations or unstable control interactions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設均勻管長L=1000m、波速a=1000m/s，往返時間2L/a=2s；只代表此單一路徑，不是允許關閉時間。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Round-trip2L/a=2s describes only this path, not an allowable closing time.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將單程時間當往返時間會改變快速與慢速的分類，忽略分岔反射則可能漏掉疊加峰值。即使動作很慢，長時間水位振盪或控制不穩定仍可能存在。","textEn":"Confusing one-way with round-trip time changes the rapid-action classification, while omitted branch reflections can hide superposed peaks. Slow actuation can still produce long-period level oscillations or unstable control interactions.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「往返時間與邊界」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Round-trip time and boundaries\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。","將單程時間當往返時間會改變快速與慢速的分類，忽略分岔反射則可能漏掉疊加峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.","Confusing one-way with round-trip time changes the rapid-action classification, while omitted branch reflections can hide superposed peaks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將單程時間當往返時間會改變快速與慢速的分類，忽略分岔反射則可能漏掉疊加峰值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing one-way with round-trip time changes the rapid-action classification, while omitted branch reflections can hide superposed peaks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b260-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「快速變速壓力增量」與「井內連續方程」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rapid velocity-change pressure\" and \"Continuity within the shaft\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b260-v15-09","title":"快速變速壓力增量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rapid velocity-change pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「快速變速壓力增量」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rapid velocity-change pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"單相彈性管中的突然流速變化會形成壓力波，焦科夫斯基關係估第一個波前的壓力增量。它不是整段歷時的通用最大值，反射疊加、氣穴與控制器仍可能改變結果；應先區分增量和原有靜壓，再檢查是否仍滿足單相及快速動作假設。 假設ρ=1000kg/m³、a=1000m/s，0.5s內減速1m/s且小於2s往返，Δp=ρaΔV=1MPa，ΔH=101.94m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「快速變速壓力增量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A rapid velocity change in a single-phase elastic conduit generates a pressure wave, with the Joukowsky relation estimating the first-front increment. It is not a universal maximum for the entire history: reflections, cavities and control behavior can alter the result. Distinguish this increment from initial pressure and verify both the rapid-action and single-phase assumptions. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,a=1000m/s and velocity reduction1m/s in0.5s, shorter than2s round-trip. Initial pressure increment1MPa corresponds to101.94m head. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rapid velocity-change pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「快速變速壓力增量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rapid velocity-change pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-09-k1","title":"快速變速壓力增量","titleEn":"Rapid velocity-change pressure","text":"單相彈性管中的突然流速變化會形成壓力波，焦科夫斯基關係估第一個波前的壓力增量。它不是整段歷時的通用最大值，反射疊加、氣穴與控制器仍可能改變結果；應先區分增量和原有靜壓，再檢查是否仍滿足單相及快速動作假設。","textEn":"A rapid velocity change in a single-phase elastic conduit generates a pressure wave, with the Joukowsky relation estimating the first-front increment. It is not a universal maximum for the entire history: reflections, cavities and control behavior can alter the result.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「快速變速壓力增量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rapid velocity-change pressure\" is correct?","options":["單相彈性管中的突然流速變化會形成壓力波，焦科夫斯基關係估第一個波前的壓力增量。","焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。","瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。"],"optionsEn":["A rapid velocity change in a single-phase elastic conduit generates a pressure wave, with the Joukowsky relation estimating the first-front increment.","The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.","An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單相彈性管中的突然流速變化會形成壓力波，焦科夫斯基關係估第一個波前的壓力增量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A rapid velocity change in a single-phase elastic conduit generates a pressure wave, with the Joukowsky relation estimating the first-front increment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b260-v15-10","title":"快速變速壓力增量：定量估算","titleEn":"Rapid velocity-change pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「快速變速壓力增量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rapid velocity-change pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設ρ=1000kg/m³、a=1000m/s，0.5s內減速1m/s且小於2s往返，Δp=ρaΔV=1MPa，ΔH=101.94m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,a=1000m/s and velocity reduction1m/s in0.5s, shorter than2s round-trip. Initial pressure increment1MPa corresponds to101.94m head. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設ρ=1000kg/m³、a=1000m/s，0.5s內減速1m/s且小於2s往返，Δp=ρaΔV=1MPa，ΔH=101.94m。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,a=1000m/s and velocity reduction1m/s in0.5s, shorter than2s round-trip. Initial pressure increment1MPa corresponds to101.94m head.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「快速變速壓力增量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rapid velocity-change pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。"],"optionsEn":["The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b260-v15-11","title":"快速變速壓力增量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rapid velocity-change pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「快速變速壓力增量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rapid velocity-change pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。將第一波預估和完整瞬態歷時比較，另查後續反射最低壓力、局部空化及機組反應，不把首波算式視為完整包絡。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration. Compare the first-wave estimate with a full transient history and separately examine reflected minima, local cavitation and machine response rather than treating the first front as the complete envelope. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。將第一波預估和完整瞬態歷時比較，另查後續反射最低壓力、局部空化及機組反應，不把首波算式視為完整包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration. Compare the first-wave estimate with a full transient history and separately examine reflected minima, local cavitation and machine response rather than treating the first front as the complete envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：把壓力增量當成總壓力會漏掉原有水頭，慢關閉時套完整瞬降公式又可能錯估反應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating the increment as total pressure omits the initial head, while applying instantaneous reduction to slow closure misrepresents the response. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。將第一波預估和完整瞬態歷時比較，另查後續反射最低壓力、局部空化及機組反應，不把首波算式視為完整包絡。","textEn":"State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration. Compare the first-wave estimate with a full transient history and separately examine reflected minima, local cavitation and machine response rather than treating the first front as the complete envelope.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。將第一波預估和完整瞬態歷時比較，另查後續反射最低壓力、局部空化及機組反應，不把首波算式視為完整包絡。","textEn":"State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration. Compare the first-wave estimate with a full transient history and separately examine reflected minima, local cavitation and machine response rather than treating the first front as the complete envelope.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「快速變速壓力增量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rapid velocity-change pressure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。","明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct.","State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b260-v15-12","title":"快速變速壓力增量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rapid velocity-change pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「快速變速壓力增量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rapid velocity-change pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把壓力增量當成總壓力會漏掉原有水頭，慢關閉時套完整瞬降公式又可能錯估反應。若發生水柱分離，重新閉合壓力不能靠原單相首波關係完整描述。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating the increment as total pressure omits the initial head, while applying instantaneous reduction to slow closure misrepresents the response. Column separation and rejoining cannot be fully described by the original single-phase first-wave relation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設ρ=1000kg/m³、a=1000m/s，0.5s內減速1m/s且小於2s往返，Δp=ρaΔV=1MPa，ΔH=101.94m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Initial pressure increment1MPa corresponds to101.94m head.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把壓力增量當成總壓力會漏掉原有水頭，慢關閉時套完整瞬降公式又可能錯估反應。若發生水柱分離，重新閉合壓力不能靠原單相首波關係完整描述。","textEn":"Treating the increment as total pressure omits the initial head, while applying instantaneous reduction to slow closure misrepresents the response. Column separation and rejoining cannot be fully described by the original single-phase first-wave relation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「快速變速壓力增量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rapid velocity-change pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把壓力增量當成總壓力會漏掉原有水頭，慢關閉時套完整瞬降公式又可能錯估反應。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。"],"optionsEn":["Treating the increment as total pressure omits the initial head, while applying instantaneous reduction to slow closure misrepresents the response.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把壓力增量當成總壓力會漏掉原有水頭，慢關閉時套完整瞬降公式又可能錯估反應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating the increment as total pressure omits the initial head, while applying instantaneous reduction to slow closure misrepresents the response. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b260-v15-13","title":"井內連續方程：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Continuity within the shaft: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「井內連續方程」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Continuity within the shaft” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"調壓井提供暫時儲水空間，管內來水與下游取水不相等時便改變井內水位。這個體積平衡不需要先求水錘峰值，但流量差本身會隨水位與管內慣性變化；固定面積只能用在井身相應區段，不能把瞬時上升速率無限制外推。 假設井面積100m²、瞬時流入20及流出5m³/s，dz/dt=(20−5)/100=0.15m/s；流量差不假定長期固定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「井內連續方程」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A surge shaft temporarily stores the difference between conduit inflow and downstream demand. Volume continuity can be written before solving the pressure-wave peak, but that flow difference evolves with level and conduit inertia. Constant area applies only within the relevant shaft segment, and an instantaneous rise rate cannot be extrapolated indefinitely through the entire transient. Assume shaft area100m² with instantaneous inflow20 and outflow5m³/s. Rise ratedz/dt=0.15m/s does not assume that imbalance persists. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Continuity within the shaft” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「井內連續方程」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Continuity within the shaft”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-13-k1","title":"井內連續方程","titleEn":"Continuity within the shaft","text":"調壓井提供暫時儲水空間，管內來水與下游取水不相等時便改變井內水位。這個體積平衡不需要先求水錘峰值，但流量差本身會隨水位與管內慣性變化；固定面積只能用在井身相應區段，不能把瞬時上升速率無限制外推。","textEn":"A surge shaft temporarily stores the difference between conduit inflow and downstream demand. Volume continuity can be written before solving the pressure-wave peak, but that flow difference evolves with level and conduit inertia.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「井內連續方程」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Continuity within the shaft\" is correct?","options":["瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。","調壓井提供暫時儲水空間，管內來水與下游取水不相等時便改變井內水位。","調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow.","A surge shaft temporarily stores the difference between conduit inflow and downstream demand.","The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"調壓井提供暫時儲水空間，管內來水與下游取水不相等時便改變井內水位。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A surge shaft temporarily stores the difference between conduit inflow and downstream demand. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b260-v15-14","title":"井內連續方程：定量估算","titleEn":"Continuity within the shaft: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「井內連續方程」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Continuity within the shaft” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設井面積100m²、瞬時流入20及流出5m³/s，dz/dt=(20−5)/100=0.15m/s；流量差不假定長期固定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume shaft area100m² with instantaneous inflow20 and outflow5m³/s. Rise ratedz/dt=0.15m/s does not assume that imbalance persists. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設井面積100m²、瞬時流入20及流出5m³/s，dz/dt=(20−5)/100=0.15m/s；流量差不假定長期固定。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume shaft area100m² with instantaneous inflow20 and outflow5m³/s. Rise ratedz/dt=0.15m/s does not assume that imbalance persists.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「井內連續方程」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Continuity within the shaft\", which statement holds?","options":["管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。","任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water.","Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b260-v15-15","title":"井內連續方程：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Continuity within the shaft: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「井內連續方程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Continuity within the shaft” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。將算出的水位回饋到管路動量方程，不把指定流量差當成與井水位完全無關的邊界。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration. Feed the updated level back into conduit momentum rather than treating the imposed imbalance as independent of shaft water level. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。將算出的水位回饋到管路動量方程，不把指定流量差當成與井水位完全無關的邊界。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration. Feed the updated level back into conduit momentum rather than treating the imposed imbalance as independent of shaft water level.","failure":"注意干擾：面積使用直徑代替會破壞量綱，井身變截面時固定面積又會誤估上升速度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Substituting diameter for area breaks dimensional consistency, while changing shaft sections invalidate a fixed-area rate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。將算出的水位回饋到管路動量方程，不把指定流量差當成與井水位完全無關的邊界。","textEn":"Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration. Feed the updated level back into conduit momentum rather than treating the imposed imbalance as independent of shaft water level.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。將算出的水位回饋到管路動量方程，不把指定流量差當成與井水位完全無關的邊界。","textEn":"Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration. Feed the updated level back into conduit momentum rather than treating the imposed imbalance as independent of shaft water level.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「井內連續方程」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Continuity within the shaft\"?","options":["將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。"],"optionsEn":["Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b260-v15-16","title":"井內連續方程：失效診斷","titleEn":"Continuity within the shaft: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「井內連續方程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Continuity within the shaft” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"面積使用直徑代替會破壞量綱，井身變截面時固定面積又會誤估上升速度。只積分入流不扣下游流量，會虛增儲水並製造不存在的溢井預測。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Substituting diameter for area breaks dimensional consistency, while changing shaft sections invalidate a fixed-area rate. Integrating inflow without subtracting downstream flow invents storage and can predict a shaft overflow that the stated balance does not support. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設井面積100m²、瞬時流入20及流出5m³/s，dz/dt=(20−5)/100=0.15m/s；流量差不假定長期固定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Rise ratedz/dt=0.15m/s does not assume that imbalance persists.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"面積使用直徑代替會破壞量綱，井身變截面時固定面積又會誤估上升速度。只積分入流不扣下游流量，會虛增儲水並製造不存在的溢井預測。","textEn":"Substituting diameter for area breaks dimensional consistency, while changing shaft sections invalidate a fixed-area rate. Integrating inflow without subtracting downstream flow invents storage and can predict a shaft overflow that the stated balance does not support.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「井內連續方程」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Continuity within the shaft\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","面積使用直徑代替會破壞量綱，井身變截面時固定面積又會誤估上升速度。","調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Substituting diameter for area breaks dimensional consistency, while changing shaft sections invalidate a fixed-area rate.","The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"面積使用直徑代替會破壞量綱，井身變截面時固定面積又會誤估上升速度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Substituting diameter for area breaks dimensional consistency, while changing shaft sections invalidate a fixed-area rate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b260-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「剛性水柱振盪週期」與「理想湧升能量界限」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rigid-column oscillation period\" and \"Ideal upsurge energy estimate\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b260-v15-17","title":"剛性水柱振盪週期：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rigid-column oscillation period: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「剛性水柱振盪週期」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rigid-column oscillation period” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"較慢的井水位振盪可在特定條件下用剛性水柱近似，水柱慣性與自由水面重力形成回復系統。這與快速彈性波不同，忽略摩擦與壓縮性只為得到可核對的基準週期；實際控制器、節流口及變截面會改變衰減與穩定性。 假設定水位上庫、均勻管L=1000m及Ap=10m²、井As=100m²，無摩擦小振幅且忽略井水慣性，T=2π√(LAs/gAp)=200.607s。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剛性水柱振盪週期」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Slower shaft-level oscillation can be approximated by a rigid water column under defined conditions, with column inertia and free-surface gravity forming a restoring system. This differs from the fast elastic wave. Neglecting friction and compressibility gives a checkable reference period, while controls, throttles and variable geometry change damping and stability in the actual installation. Assume fixed reservoir level, uniform conduitL=1000m,Ap=10m² and shaftAs=100m². Frictionless small oscillations neglecting shaft inertia haveT=200.607s. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rigid-column oscillation period” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剛性水柱振盪週期」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rigid-column oscillation period”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-17-k1","title":"剛性水柱振盪週期","titleEn":"Rigid-column oscillation period","text":"較慢的井水位振盪可在特定條件下用剛性水柱近似，水柱慣性與自由水面重力形成回復系統。這與快速彈性波不同，忽略摩擦與壓縮性只為得到可核對的基準週期；實際控制器、節流口及變截面會改變衰減與穩定性。","textEn":"Slower shaft-level oscillation can be approximated by a rigid water column under defined conditions, with column inertia and free-surface gravity forming a restoring system. This differs from the fast elastic wave.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「剛性水柱振盪週期」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rigid-column oscillation period\" is correct?","options":["調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。","理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","較慢的井水位振盪可在特定條件下用剛性水柱近似，水柱慣性與自由水面重力形成回復系統。"],"optionsEn":["The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time.","The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","Slower shaft-level oscillation can be approximated by a rigid water column under defined conditions, with column inertia and free-surface gravity forming a restoring system."],"answer":2,"explanation":"較慢的井水位振盪可在特定條件下用剛性水柱近似，水柱慣性與自由水面重力形成回復系統。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Slower shaft-level oscillation can be approximated by a rigid water column under defined conditions, with column inertia and free-surface gravity forming a restoring system. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b260-v15-18","title":"剛性水柱振盪週期：定量估算","titleEn":"Rigid-column oscillation period: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剛性水柱振盪週期」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rigid-column oscillation period” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設定水位上庫、均勻管L=1000m及Ap=10m²、井As=100m²，無摩擦小振幅且忽略井水慣性，T=2π√(LAs/gAp)=200.607s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume fixed reservoir level, uniform conduitL=1000m,Ap=10m² and shaftAs=100m². Frictionless small oscillations neglecting shaft inertia haveT=200.607s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設定水位上庫、均勻管L=1000m及Ap=10m²、井As=100m²，無摩擦小振幅且忽略井水慣性，T=2π√(LAs/gAp)=200.607s。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume fixed reservoir level, uniform conduitL=1000m,Ap=10m² and shaftAs=100m². Frictionless small oscillations neglecting shaft inertia haveT=200.607s.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「剛性水柱振盪週期」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rigid-column oscillation period\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。","Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system.","A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b260-v15-19","title":"剛性水柱振盪週期：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rigid-column oscillation period: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剛性水柱振盪週期」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rigid-column oscillation period” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。以小擾動數值解比較解析週期，再逐步加入摩擦、井水慣性與控制器，標註每次加入機制後的週期及衰減差異。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units. Compare an analytical period with a small-disturbance numerical solution, then add friction, shaft inertia and controls separately, recording changes in period and damping. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。以小擾動數值解比較解析週期，再逐步加入摩擦、井水慣性與控制器，標註每次加入機制後的週期及衰減差異。","observationEn":"Site practice: Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units. Compare an analytical period with a small-disturbance numerical solution, then add friction, shaft inertia and controls separately, recording changes in period and damping.","failure":"注意干擾：用此長週期代替壓力波往返時間會漏掉早期水錘，忽略機組控制又可能看不到自激振盪。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using this long period in place of wave travel time misses early water hammer, and omitted machine control can hide self-excitation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。以小擾動數值解比較解析週期，再逐步加入摩擦、井水慣性與控制器，標註每次加入機制後的週期及衰減差異。","textEn":"Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units. Compare an analytical period with a small-disturbance numerical solution, then add friction, shaft inertia and controls separately, recording changes in period and damping.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。以小擾動數值解比較解析週期，再逐步加入摩擦、井水慣性與控制器，標註每次加入機制後的週期及衰減差異。","textEn":"Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units. Compare an analytical period with a small-disturbance numerical solution, then add friction, shaft inertia and controls separately, recording changes in period and damping.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「剛性水柱振盪週期」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rigid-column oscillation period\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。","閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units.","An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b260-v15-20","title":"剛性水柱振盪週期：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rigid-column oscillation period: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剛性水柱振盪週期」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rigid-column oscillation period” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用此長週期代替壓力波往返時間會漏掉早期水錘，忽略機組控制又可能看不到自激振盪。模型沒有耗散時持續振動是其假設結果，不能當成實際阻尼證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using this long period in place of wave travel time misses early water hammer, and omitted machine control can hide self-excitation. Persistent motion in a lossless model follows its assumptions and does not measure real-system damping. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設定水位上庫、均勻管L=1000m及Ap=10m²、井As=100m²，無摩擦小振幅且忽略井水慣性，T=2π√(LAs/gAp)=200.607s。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Frictionless small oscillations neglecting shaft inertia haveT=200.607s.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用此長週期代替壓力波往返時間會漏掉早期水錘，忽略機組控制又可能看不到自激振盪。模型沒有耗散時持續振動是其假設結果，不能當成實際阻尼證據。","textEn":"Using this long period in place of wave travel time misses early water hammer, and omitted machine control can hide self-excitation. Persistent motion in a lossless model follows its assumptions and does not measure real-system damping.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剛性水柱振盪週期」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rigid-column oscillation period\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","用此長週期代替壓力波往返時間會漏掉早期水錘，忽略機組控制又可能看不到自激振盪。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","Using this long period in place of wave travel time misses early water hammer, and omitted machine control can hide self-excitation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用此長週期代替壓力波往返時間會漏掉早期水錘，忽略機組控制又可能看不到自激振盪。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using this long period in place of wave travel time misses early water hammer, and omitted machine control can hide self-excitation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b260-v15-21","title":"理想湧升能量界限：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ideal upsurge energy estimate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「理想湧升能量界限」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ideal upsurge energy estimate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"突然停止下游取水後，管內水柱動能可轉為井中水位上升的位能，提供無損理想基準。必須把井位移相對於固定水庫水面定義，並說明初始水位偏差；忽略摩擦、井水慣性與壓力彈性能量時，結果不能視為實際溢流高度的完整設計包絡。 假設初始井位等於固定庫位、L=1000m、Ap=10m²、As=100m²、V0=2m/s，瞬停下游且無損，zmax=V0√(LAp/gAs)=6.3855m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「理想湧升能量界限」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After downstream demand stops, conduit kinetic energy can become potential energy in a rising shaft, giving a lossless reference. Define displacement relative to the fixed reservoir surface and specify the initial level offset. When friction, shaft inertia and elastic-wave energy are omitted, the estimate cannot serve as a complete design envelope for actual overflow height. Assume initial shaft level equals fixed reservoir level,L=1000m,Ap=10m²,As=100m²,V0=2m/s and instantaneous demand stop. Lossless rigid-columnzmax=6.3855m. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ideal upsurge energy estimate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「理想湧升能量界限」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ideal upsurge energy estimate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-21-k1","title":"理想湧升能量界限","titleEn":"Ideal upsurge energy estimate","text":"突然停止下游取水後，管內水柱動能可轉為井中水位上升的位能，提供無損理想基準。必須把井位移相對於固定水庫水面定義，並說明初始水位偏差；忽略摩擦、井水慣性與壓力彈性能量時，結果不能視為實際溢流高度的完整設計包絡。","textEn":"After downstream demand stops, conduit kinetic energy can become potential energy in a rising shaft, giving a lossless reference. Define displacement relative to the fixed reservoir surface and specify the initial level offset.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「理想湧升能量界限」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ideal upsurge energy estimate\" is correct?","options":["突然停止下游取水後，管內水柱動能可轉為井中水位上升的位能，提供無損理想基準。","理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。"],"optionsEn":["After downstream demand stops, conduit kinetic energy can become potential energy in a rising shaft, giving a lossless reference.","The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water."],"answer":0,"explanation":"突然停止下游取水後，管內水柱動能可轉為井中水位上升的位能，提供無損理想基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After downstream demand stops, conduit kinetic energy can become potential energy in a rising shaft, giving a lossless reference. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b260-v15-22","title":"理想湧升能量界限：定量估算","titleEn":"Ideal upsurge energy estimate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「理想湧升能量界限」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ideal upsurge energy estimate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設初始井位等於固定庫位、L=1000m、Ap=10m²、As=100m²、V0=2m/s，瞬停下游且無損，zmax=V0√(LAp/gAs)=6.3855m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume initial shaft level equals fixed reservoir level,L=1000m,Ap=10m²,As=100m²,V0=2m/s and instantaneous demand stop. Lossless rigid-columnzmax=6.3855m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設初始井位等於固定庫位、L=1000m、Ap=10m²、As=100m²、V0=2m/s，瞬停下游且無損，zmax=V0√(LAp/gAs)=6.3855m。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume initial shaft level equals fixed reservoir level,L=1000m,Ap=10m²,As=100m²,V0=2m/s and instantaneous demand stop. Lossless rigid-columnzmax=6.3855m.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「理想湧升能量界限」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ideal upsurge energy estimate\", which statement holds?","options":["任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。"],"optionsEn":["Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b260-v15-23","title":"理想湧升能量界限：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ideal upsurge energy estimate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「理想湧升能量界限」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ideal upsurge energy estimate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。再用動量連續方程數值解對照，另測非零初始偏差、損失和彈性波對最高及最低水位的影響。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset. Compare with coupled momentum-continuity integration, then separately test nonzero initial offset, loss and elastic-wave effects on both maximum and minimum levels. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。再用動量連續方程數值解對照，另測非零初始偏差、損失和彈性波對最高及最低水位的影響。","observationEn":"Site practice: Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset. Compare with coupled momentum-continuity integration, then separately test nonzero initial offset, loss and elastic-wave effects on both maximum and minimum levels.","failure":"注意干擾：初始井水位若已因摩擦低於庫位，直接套零偏差公式會遺漏能量項。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An initial shaft level depressed by friction requires an additional energy term. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。再用動量連續方程數值解對照，另測非零初始偏差、損失和彈性波對最高及最低水位的影響。","textEn":"Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset. Compare with coupled momentum-continuity integration, then separately test nonzero initial offset, loss and elastic-wave effects on both maximum and minimum levels.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。再用動量連續方程數值解對照，另測非零初始偏差、損失和彈性波對最高及最低水位的影響。","textEn":"Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset. Compare with coupled momentum-continuity integration, then separately test nonzero initial offset, loss and elastic-wave effects on both maximum and minimum levels.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「理想湧升能量界限」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ideal upsurge energy estimate\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。","寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.","Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset."],"answer":2,"explanation":"寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b260-v15-24","title":"理想湧升能量界限：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ideal upsurge energy estimate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「理想湧升能量界限」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ideal upsurge energy estimate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"初始井水位若已因摩擦低於庫位，直接套零偏差公式會遺漏能量項。把無損湧升直接當允許井高也會忽略自由高、通氣與更複雜邊界造成的變化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An initial shaft level depressed by friction requires an additional energy term. Treating the lossless rise as an allowable shaft height also omits freeboard, ventilation and changes caused by more complex boundaries. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設初始井位等於固定庫位、L=1000m、Ap=10m²、As=100m²、V0=2m/s，瞬停下游且無損，zmax=V0√(LAp/gAs)=6.3855m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Lossless rigid-columnzmax=6.3855m.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"初始井水位若已因摩擦低於庫位，直接套零偏差公式會遺漏能量項。把無損湧升直接當允許井高也會忽略自由高、通氣與更複雜邊界造成的變化。","textEn":"An initial shaft level depressed by friction requires an additional energy term. Treating the lossless rise as an allowable shaft height also omits freeboard, ventilation and changes caused by more complex boundaries.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「理想湧升能量界限」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ideal upsurge energy estimate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["初始井水位若已因摩擦低於庫位，直接套零偏差公式會遺漏能量項。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。"],"optionsEn":["An initial shaft level depressed by friction requires an additional energy term.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water."],"answer":0,"explanation":"初始井水位若已因摩擦低於庫位，直接套零偏差公式會遺漏能量項。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An initial shaft level depressed by friction requires an additional energy term. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b260-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「沿程摩擦與耗散」與「節流孔與局部損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Distributed friction and dissipation\" and \"Throttle opening and local loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b260-v15-25","title":"沿程摩擦與耗散：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Distributed friction and dissipation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「沿程摩擦與耗散」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Distributed friction and dissipation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"管壁摩擦耗散能量並影響井水振盪衰減，穩態摩擦式可作第一層準穩態近似。反向流動時損失應反向抵抗速度，不能永遠沿固定坐標扣水頭；快速瞬態的非穩態摩擦則可能需要額外模型，不能只靠增大摩擦係數修正錯誤結果。 假設Darcy摩擦係數0.02、管長1000m、直徑2m、速率2m/s，hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m，僅為此工況準穩態損失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沿程摩擦與耗散」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wall friction dissipates energy and influences surge decay, with a steady relation serving as a first quasi-steady approximation. During flow reversal the loss must oppose velocity rather than remain fixed in one coordinate direction. Rapid transients may require unsteady friction, which should not be replaced by arbitrarily increasing a coefficient to compensate for an incorrect model. Assume Darcy factor0.02,length1000m,diameter2m and speed2m/s. Quasi-steady loss hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m at this condition. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Distributed friction and dissipation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沿程摩擦與耗散」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Distributed friction and dissipation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-25-k1","title":"沿程摩擦與耗散","titleEn":"Distributed friction and dissipation","text":"管壁摩擦耗散能量並影響井水振盪衰減，穩態摩擦式可作第一層準穩態近似。反向流動時損失應反向抵抗速度，不能永遠沿固定坐標扣水頭；快速瞬態的非穩態摩擦則可能需要額外模型，不能只靠增大摩擦係數修正錯誤結果。","textEn":"Wall friction dissipates energy and influences surge decay, with a steady relation serving as a first quasi-steady approximation. During flow reversal the loss must oppose velocity rather than remain fixed in one coordinate direction.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沿程摩擦與耗散」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Distributed friction and dissipation\" is correct?","options":["管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。","管壁摩擦耗散能量並影響井水振盪衰減，穩態摩擦式可作第一層準穩態近似。","節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。"],"optionsEn":["During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water.","Wall friction dissipates energy and influences surge decay, with a steady relation serving as a first quasi-steady approximation.","A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system."],"answer":1,"explanation":"管壁摩擦耗散能量並影響井水振盪衰減，穩態摩擦式可作第一層準穩態近似。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wall friction dissipates energy and influences surge decay, with a steady relation serving as a first quasi-steady approximation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b260-v15-26","title":"沿程摩擦與耗散：定量估算","titleEn":"Distributed friction and dissipation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沿程摩擦與耗散」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Distributed friction and dissipation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設Darcy摩擦係數0.02、管長1000m、直徑2m、速率2m/s，hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m，僅為此工況準穩態損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume Darcy factor0.02,length1000m,diameter2m and speed2m/s. Quasi-steady loss hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m at this condition. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設Darcy摩擦係數0.02、管長1000m、直徑2m、速率2m/s，hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m，僅為此工況準穩態損失。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume Darcy factor0.02,length1000m,diameter2m and speed2m/s. Quasi-steady loss hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m at this condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沿程摩擦與耗散」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Distributed friction and dissipation\", which statement holds?","options":["Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。","閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct.","An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b260-v15-27","title":"沿程摩擦與耗散：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Distributed friction and dissipation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沿程摩擦與耗散」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Distributed friction and dissipation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。將摩擦寫成抵抗流向的V乘絕對V形式，檢查流向反轉時仍耗能，再比較不同摩擦模型對衰減歷時的影響。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions. Express directional friction using velocity times its magnitude, verify dissipation during reversal and compare how alternative friction representations change the decay history. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。將摩擦寫成抵抗流向的V乘絕對V形式，檢查流向反轉時仍耗能，再比較不同摩擦模型對衰減歷時的影響。","observationEn":"Site practice: Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions. Express directional friction using velocity times its magnitude, verify dissipation during reversal and compare how alternative friction representations change the decay history.","failure":"注意干擾：混淆兩種摩擦係數可造成四倍差異，流向反轉後符號不改更可能讓摩擦虛假供能。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing friction conventions introduces a factor-of-four error, and the wrong reversal sign can make friction supply energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。將摩擦寫成抵抗流向的V乘絕對V形式，檢查流向反轉時仍耗能，再比較不同摩擦模型對衰減歷時的影響。","textEn":"Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions. Express directional friction using velocity times its magnitude, verify dissipation during reversal and compare how alternative friction representations change the decay history.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。將摩擦寫成抵抗流向的V乘絕對V形式，檢查流向反轉時仍耗能，再比較不同摩擦模型對衰減歷時的影響。","textEn":"Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions. Express directional friction using velocity times its magnitude, verify dissipation during reversal and compare how alternative friction representations change the decay history.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沿程摩擦與耗散」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Distributed friction and dissipation\"?","options":["註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。"],"optionsEn":["Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b260-v15-28","title":"沿程摩擦與耗散：失效診斷","titleEn":"Distributed friction and dissipation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沿程摩擦與耗散」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Distributed friction and dissipation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"混淆兩種摩擦係數可造成四倍差異，流向反轉後符號不改更可能讓摩擦虛假供能。以強阻尼掩蓋時間步誤差，會讓看似平順的曲線失去物理可信度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing friction conventions introduces a factor-of-four error, and the wrong reversal sign can make friction supply energy. Artificial damping that hides time-step errors yields smooth-looking curves without reliable physical meaning. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設Darcy摩擦係數0.02、管長1000m、直徑2m、速率2m/s，hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m，僅為此工況準穩態損失。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Quasi-steady loss hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m at this condition.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"混淆兩種摩擦係數可造成四倍差異，流向反轉後符號不改更可能讓摩擦虛假供能。以強阻尼掩蓋時間步誤差，會讓看似平順的曲線失去物理可信度。","textEn":"Confusing friction conventions introduces a factor-of-four error, and the wrong reversal sign can make friction supply energy. Artificial damping that hides time-step errors yields smooth-looking curves without reliable physical meaning.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沿程摩擦與耗散」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Distributed friction and dissipation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","混淆兩種摩擦係數可造成四倍差異，流向反轉後符號不改更可能讓摩擦虛假供能。","節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Confusing friction conventions introduces a factor-of-four error, and the wrong reversal sign can make friction supply energy.","A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system."],"answer":1,"explanation":"混淆兩種摩擦係數可造成四倍差異，流向反轉後符號不改更可能讓摩擦虛假供能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing friction conventions introduces a factor-of-four error, and the wrong reversal sign can make friction supply energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b260-v15-29","title":"節流孔與局部損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Throttle opening and local loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「節流孔與局部損失」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Throttle opening and local loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"節流可改變井與主管之間的交換及耗散，但更大阻力不保證所有壓力峰值都下降。孔口附近的局部低壓、流向切換和收縮係數需要另外檢查；準穩態孔流關係只描述指定瞬間的流量水頭差，不能直接取代完整調壓設施的瞬態模型。 假設孔口Q=10m³/s、Cd=0.65、有效面積2m²，水頭差h=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m；未驗局部空化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「節流孔與局部損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A throttle changes exchange and dissipation between shaft and conduit, but increased resistance does not guarantee lower pressure peaks everywhere. Local suction, reversal and contraction behavior require separate checks. A quasi-steady orifice relation describes one flow-head condition and cannot replace a transient model of the complete surge arrangement and its connected waterway. Assume orifice flow10m³/s, coefficient0.65 and effective area2m². Head differenceh=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m, without evaluating local cavitation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Throttle opening and local loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「節流孔與局部損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Throttle opening and local loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-29-k1","title":"節流孔與局部損失","titleEn":"Throttle opening and local loss","text":"節流可改變井與主管之間的交換及耗散，但更大阻力不保證所有壓力峰值都下降。孔口附近的局部低壓、流向切換和收縮係數需要另外檢查；準穩態孔流關係只描述指定瞬間的流量水頭差，不能直接取代完整調壓設施的瞬態模型。","textEn":"A throttle changes exchange and dissipation between shaft and conduit, but increased resistance does not guarantee lower pressure peaks everywhere. Local suction, reversal and contraction behavior require separate checks.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「節流孔與局部損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Throttle opening and local loss\" is correct?","options":["節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。","任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。","節流可改變井與主管之間的交換及耗散，但更大阻力不保證所有壓力峰值都下降。"],"optionsEn":["A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system.","Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.","A throttle changes exchange and dissipation between shaft and conduit, but increased resistance does not guarantee lower pressure peaks everywhere."],"answer":2,"explanation":"節流可改變井與主管之間的交換及耗散，但更大阻力不保證所有壓力峰值都下降。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A throttle changes exchange and dissipation between shaft and conduit, but increased resistance does not guarantee lower pressure peaks everywhere. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b260-v15-30","title":"節流孔與局部損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Throttle opening and local loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「節流孔與局部損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Throttle opening and local loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設孔口Q=10m³/s、Cd=0.65、有效面積2m²，水頭差h=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m；未驗局部空化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume orifice flow10m³/s, coefficient0.65 and effective area2m². Head differenceh=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m, without evaluating local cavitation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設孔口Q=10m³/s、Cd=0.65、有效面積2m²，水頭差h=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m；未驗局部空化。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume orifice flow10m³/s, coefficient0.65 and effective area2m². Head differenceh=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m, without evaluating local cavitation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「節流孔與局部損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Throttle opening and local loss\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。","焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas.","The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b260-v15-31","title":"節流孔與局部損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Throttle opening and local loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「節流孔與局部損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Throttle opening and local loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。比較入井與出井的壓差資料，將孔口關係接入動量及連續方程，再檢查最低絕對壓力與反向流條件而非只看耗能增加。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area. Compare inward and outward pressure differences, couple the opening relation to momentum and continuity and inspect minimum absolute pressure and reversal rather than only increased dissipation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。比較入井與出井的壓差資料，將孔口關係接入動量及連續方程，再檢查最低絕對壓力與反向流條件而非只看耗能增加。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area. Compare inward and outward pressure differences, couple the opening relation to momentum and continuity and inspect minimum absolute pressure and reversal rather than only increased dissipation.","failure":"注意干擾：孔口太小可能限制快速交換而提高主管壓力，收縮區低壓也可能造成空化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An overly restrictive opening can hinder rapid exchange and raise conduit pressure, while a contracted jet can cavitate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。比較入井與出井的壓差資料，將孔口關係接入動量及連續方程，再檢查最低絕對壓力與反向流條件而非只看耗能增加。","textEn":"Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area. Compare inward and outward pressure differences, couple the opening relation to momentum and continuity and inspect minimum absolute pressure and reversal rather than only increased dissipation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。比較入井與出井的壓差資料，將孔口關係接入動量及連續方程，再檢查最低絕對壓力與反向流條件而非只看耗能增加。","textEn":"Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area. Compare inward and outward pressure differences, couple the opening relation to momentum and continuity and inspect minimum absolute pressure and reversal rather than only increased dissipation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「節流孔與局部損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Throttle opening and local loss\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。","調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area.","The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b260-v15-32","title":"節流孔與局部損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Throttle opening and local loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「節流孔與局部損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Throttle opening and local loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"孔口太小可能限制快速交換而提高主管壓力，收縮區低壓也可能造成空化。直接用同一係數描述兩個方向，會漏掉非對稱構造引起的不同水頭損失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An overly restrictive opening can hinder rapid exchange and raise conduit pressure, while a contracted jet can cavitate. Applying one coefficient to both directions misses asymmetric losses caused by the actual opening arrangement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設孔口Q=10m³/s、Cd=0.65、有效面積2m²，水頭差h=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m；未驗局部空化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head differenceh=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m, without evaluating local cavitation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"孔口太小可能限制快速交換而提高主管壓力，收縮區低壓也可能造成空化。直接用同一係數描述兩個方向，會漏掉非對稱構造引起的不同水頭損失。","textEn":"An overly restrictive opening can hinder rapid exchange and raise conduit pressure, while a contracted jet can cavitate. Applying one coefficient to both directions misses asymmetric losses caused by the actual opening arrangement.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「節流孔與局部損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Throttle opening and local loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。","孔口太小可能限制快速交換而提高主管壓力，收縮區低壓也可能造成空化。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.","An overly restrictive opening can hinder rapid exchange and raise conduit pressure, while a contracted jet can cavitate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔口太小可能限制快速交換而提高主管壓力，收縮區低壓也可能造成空化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An overly restrictive opening can hinder rapid exchange and raise conduit pressure, while a contracted jet can cavitate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b260-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「絕對壓力與汽化」與「特徵網格與收斂」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Absolute pressure and vapor formation\" and \"Characteristic grid and convergence\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b260-v15-33","title":"絕對壓力與汽化：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor formation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「絕對壓力與汽化」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Absolute pressure and vapor formation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"負表壓不等於汽化，必須加上當地大氣壓後與相應溫度的蒸氣壓比較。即使某測點高於蒸氣壓，附近收縮區或未量到的瞬態仍可能更低；水柱分離涉及兩相或氣穴模型，不能把單相計算得到的不合理低壓照單全收。 假設大氣壓100kPa、表壓−80kPa、蒸氣壓2.34kPa，絕對壓20kPa，比蒸氣壓高17.66kPa；只代表該點該時刻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「絕對壓力與汽化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Negative gauge pressure is not itself vapor formation; add local atmospheric pressure and compare against vapor pressure at the relevant temperature. A measured point above vapor pressure does not exclude lower local or unresolved transient values. Column separation requires appropriate cavity or multiphase treatment rather than accepting physically impossible pressures from a single-phase computation. Assume atmospheric100kPa,gauge−80kPa and vapor pressure2.34kPa. Absolute pressure20kPa exceeds vapor by17.66kPa only at that location and instant. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Absolute pressure and vapor formation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「絕對壓力與汽化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Absolute pressure and vapor formation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-33-k1","title":"絕對壓力與汽化","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor formation","text":"負表壓不等於汽化，必須加上當地大氣壓後與相應溫度的蒸氣壓比較。即使某測點高於蒸氣壓，附近收縮區或未量到的瞬態仍可能更低；水柱分離涉及兩相或氣穴模型，不能把單相計算得到的不合理低壓照單全收。","textEn":"Negative gauge pressure is not itself vapor formation; add local atmospheric pressure and compare against vapor pressure at the relevant temperature. A measured point above vapor pressure does not exclude lower local or unresolved transient values.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「絕對壓力與汽化」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Absolute pressure and vapor formation\" is correct?","options":["負表壓不等於汽化，必須加上當地大氣壓後與相應溫度的蒸氣壓比較。","任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。","Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Negative gauge pressure is not itself vapor formation; add local atmospheric pressure and compare against vapor pressure at the relevant temperature.","Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.","A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct."],"answer":0,"explanation":"負表壓不等於汽化，必須加上當地大氣壓後與相應溫度的蒸氣壓比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Negative gauge pressure is not itself vapor formation; add local atmospheric pressure and compare against vapor pressure at the relevant temperature. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b260-v15-34","title":"絕對壓力與汽化：定量估算","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor formation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「絕對壓力與汽化」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Absolute pressure and vapor formation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設大氣壓100kPa、表壓−80kPa、蒸氣壓2.34kPa，絕對壓20kPa，比蒸氣壓高17.66kPa；只代表該點該時刻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume atmospheric100kPa,gauge−80kPa and vapor pressure2.34kPa. Absolute pressure20kPa exceeds vapor by17.66kPa only at that location and instant. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設大氣壓100kPa、表壓−80kPa、蒸氣壓2.34kPa，絕對壓20kPa，比蒸氣壓高17.66kPa；只代表該點該時刻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume atmospheric100kPa,gauge−80kPa and vapor pressure2.34kPa. Absolute pressure20kPa exceeds vapor by17.66kPa only at that location and instant.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「絕對壓力與汽化」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Absolute pressure and vapor formation\", which statement holds?","options":["閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。"],"optionsEn":["An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b260-v15-35","title":"絕對壓力與汽化：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor formation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「絕對壓力與汽化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Absolute pressure and vapor formation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。沿整條管線檢查最低壓力歷時及高點，對低於蒸氣壓的單相結果改用適當模型，並保留未解析局部區域的限制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references. Inspect minimum histories and high points along the full conduit, replace invalid single-phase predictions with suitable models and retain limitations for unresolved local regions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。沿整條管線檢查最低壓力歷時及高點，對低於蒸氣壓的單相結果改用適當模型，並保留未解析局部區域的限制。","observationEn":"Site practice: Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references. Inspect minimum histories and high points along the full conduit, replace invalid single-phase predictions with suitable models and retain limitations for unresolved local regions.","failure":"注意干擾：用海平面標準大氣壓代替高海拔實值會錯估餘量，稀疏取樣則可能漏掉短低壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using standard sea-level atmosphere at altitude misstates the margin, and sparse sampling can miss brief minima. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。沿整條管線檢查最低壓力歷時及高點，對低於蒸氣壓的單相結果改用適當模型，並保留未解析局部區域的限制。","textEn":"Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references. Inspect minimum histories and high points along the full conduit, replace invalid single-phase predictions with suitable models and retain limitations for unresolved local regions.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。沿整條管線檢查最低壓力歷時及高點，對低於蒸氣壓的單相結果改用適當模型，並保留未解析局部區域的限制。","textEn":"Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references. Inspect minimum histories and high points along the full conduit, replace invalid single-phase predictions with suitable models and retain limitations for unresolved local regions.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「絕對壓力與汽化」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Absolute pressure and vapor formation\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references."],"answer":2,"explanation":"確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b260-v15-36","title":"絕對壓力與汽化：失效診斷","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor formation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「絕對壓力與汽化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Absolute pressure and vapor formation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用海平面標準大氣壓代替高海拔實值會錯估餘量，稀疏取樣則可能漏掉短低壓。氣穴再閉合形成的壓力峰值也不會在只檢查原始高壓的流程中出現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using standard sea-level atmosphere at altitude misstates the margin, and sparse sampling can miss brief minima. Cavity rejoining can produce pressure peaks absent from a procedure that checks only the original high-pressure state. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設大氣壓100kPa、表壓−80kPa、蒸氣壓2.34kPa，絕對壓20kPa，比蒸氣壓高17.66kPa；只代表該點該時刻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Absolute pressure20kPa exceeds vapor by17.66kPa only at that location and instant.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用海平面標準大氣壓代替高海拔實值會錯估餘量，稀疏取樣則可能漏掉短低壓。氣穴再閉合形成的壓力峰值也不會在只檢查原始高壓的流程中出現。","textEn":"Using standard sea-level atmosphere at altitude misstates the margin, and sparse sampling can miss brief minima. Cavity rejoining can produce pressure peaks absent from a procedure that checks only the original high-pressure state.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「絕對壓力與汽化」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Absolute pressure and vapor formation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用海平面標準大氣壓代替高海拔實值會錯估餘量，稀疏取樣則可能漏掉短低壓。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Using standard sea-level atmosphere at altitude misstates the margin, and sparse sampling can miss brief minima.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用海平面標準大氣壓代替高海拔實值會錯估餘量，稀疏取樣則可能漏掉短低壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using standard sea-level atmosphere at altitude misstates the margin, and sparse sampling can miss brief minima. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b260-v15-37","title":"特徵網格與收斂：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Characteristic grid and convergence: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「特徵網格與收斂」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Characteristic grid and convergence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"瞬態數值解需要把傳播速度、空間網格與時間步配合，否則波前可能被過度擴散或錯置。特徵線恰好落在網格點是便利條件，並不是邊界、摩擦或兩相處理都正確的證明；必須用可解析基準及細化比較檢查壓力峰值、到時和守恆。 假設a=1000m/s、Δx=100m、Δt=0.10s，Courant數aΔt/Δx=1；只對此均勻網格特徵到點，不是完整精度證明。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「特徵網格與收斂」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Transient calculations coordinate wave speed, spatial grid and time step to avoid misplaced or excessively diffused fronts. Characteristics landing on grid points is convenient, not proof that boundaries, friction and cavities are handled correctly. Analytical benchmarks and refinement comparisons must check peak pressure, arrival time and conservation as separate aspects of numerical credibility. Assumea=1000m/s,spacing100m and step0.10s. Courant number1 aligns characteristics on this uniform grid but does not prove full accuracy. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Characteristic grid and convergence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「特徵網格與收斂」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Characteristic grid and convergence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-37-k1","title":"特徵網格與收斂","titleEn":"Characteristic grid and convergence","text":"瞬態數值解需要把傳播速度、空間網格與時間步配合，否則波前可能被過度擴散或錯置。特徵線恰好落在網格點是便利條件，並不是邊界、摩擦或兩相處理都正確的證明；必須用可解析基準及細化比較檢查壓力峰值、到時和守恆。","textEn":"Transient calculations coordinate wave speed, spatial grid and time step to avoid misplaced or excessively diffused fronts. Characteristics landing on grid points is convenient, not proof that boundaries, friction and cavities are handled correctly.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「特徵網格與收斂」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Characteristic grid and convergence\" is correct?","options":["Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。","瞬態數值解需要把傳播速度、空間網格與時間步配合，否則波前可能被過度擴散或錯置。","水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。"],"optionsEn":["A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct.","Transient calculations coordinate wave speed, spatial grid and time step to avoid misplaced or excessively diffused fronts.","Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas."],"answer":1,"explanation":"瞬態數值解需要把傳播速度、空間網格與時間步配合，否則波前可能被過度擴散或錯置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Transient calculations coordinate wave speed, spatial grid and time step to avoid misplaced or excessively diffused fronts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b260-v15-38","title":"特徵網格與收斂：定量估算","titleEn":"Characteristic grid and convergence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「特徵網格與收斂」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Characteristic grid and convergence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設a=1000m/s、Δx=100m、Δt=0.10s，Courant數aΔt/Δx=1；只對此均勻網格特徵到點，不是完整精度證明。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumea=1000m/s,spacing100m and step0.10s. Courant number1 aligns characteristics on this uniform grid but does not prove full accuracy. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設a=1000m/s、Δx=100m、Δt=0.10s，Courant數aΔt/Δx=1；只對此均勻網格特徵到點，不是完整精度證明。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumea=1000m/s,spacing100m and step0.10s. Courant number1 aligns characteristics on this uniform grid but does not prove full accuracy.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「特徵網格與收斂」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Characteristic grid and convergence\", which statement holds?","options":["焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。","調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.","The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b260-v15-39","title":"特徵網格與收斂：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Characteristic grid and convergence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「特徵網格與收斂」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Characteristic grid and convergence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。對各支管核對波速與網格，檢查質量殘差及邊界更新順序，記錄收斂而非只呈現平滑曲線。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival. Check every branch’s celerity and grid, mass residual and boundary-update sequence, documenting convergence rather than merely presenting smooth plots. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。對各支管核對波速與網格，檢查質量殘差及邊界更新順序，記錄收斂而非只呈現平滑曲線。","observationEn":"Site practice: Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival. Check every branch’s celerity and grid, mass residual and boundary-update sequence, documenting convergence rather than merely presenting smooth plots.","failure":"注意干擾：光滑曲線可能只是數值耗散抹掉了尖峰，Courant數正確也不能修復錯誤閥門邊界。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A smooth curve may reflect numerical damping that erased a peak, and correct Courant number cannot repair an incorrect valve boundary. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。對各支管核對波速與網格，檢查質量殘差及邊界更新順序，記錄收斂而非只呈現平滑曲線。","textEn":"Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival. Check every branch’s celerity and grid, mass residual and boundary-update sequence, documenting convergence rather than merely presenting smooth plots.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。對各支管核對波速與網格，檢查質量殘差及邊界更新順序，記錄收斂而非只呈現平滑曲線。","textEn":"Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival. Check every branch’s celerity and grid, mass residual and boundary-update sequence, documenting convergence rather than merely presenting smooth plots.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「特徵網格與收斂」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Characteristic grid and convergence\"?","options":["先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。"],"optionsEn":["Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b260-v15-40","title":"特徵網格與收斂：失效診斷","titleEn":"Characteristic grid and convergence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「特徵網格與收斂」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Characteristic grid and convergence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"光滑曲線可能只是數值耗散抹掉了尖峰，Courant數正確也不能修復錯誤閥門邊界。若網格改變就讓峰值大幅移動，未收斂結果不應被包裝成確定的壓力包絡。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A smooth curve may reflect numerical damping that erased a peak, and correct Courant number cannot repair an incorrect valve boundary. Peaks that move materially under refinement indicate an unconverged result rather than a definitive pressure envelope. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設a=1000m/s、Δx=100m、Δt=0.10s，Courant數aΔt/Δx=1；只對此均勻網格特徵到點，不是完整精度證明。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Courant number1 aligns characteristics on this uniform grid but does not prove full accuracy.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"光滑曲線可能只是數值耗散抹掉了尖峰，Courant數正確也不能修復錯誤閥門邊界。若網格改變就讓峰值大幅移動，未收斂結果不應被包裝成確定的壓力包絡。","textEn":"A smooth curve may reflect numerical damping that erased a peak, and correct Courant number cannot repair an incorrect valve boundary. Peaks that move materially under refinement indicate an unconverged result rather than a definitive pressure envelope.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「特徵網格與收斂」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Characteristic grid and convergence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","光滑曲線可能只是數值耗散抹掉了尖峰，Courant數正確也不能修復錯誤閥門邊界。","水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A smooth curve may reflect numerical damping that erased a peak, and correct Courant number cannot repair an incorrect valve boundary.","Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光滑曲線可能只是數值耗散抹掉了尖峰，Courant數正確也不能修復錯誤閥門邊界。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A smooth curve may reflect numerical damping that erased a peak, and correct Courant number cannot repair an incorrect valve boundary. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
